A||N||25||FieroSTETZ||one throttle per cylinder||||1||
Z||000000||FieroSTETZ||08-14-2001||01:48 AM||||i was wondering if you could do something like this (saw a ferrari w/ one carb per cylinder) you got 6 small throttle bodies, and made your own intake manifold, and had one throttle body per cylinder- this would be cool- it would be neat to have 6 trumpets sticking out of the decklid, or haveing six throttles opening and closing in a synchronized manner- am i retarted, or would this work/be cool- could probably use bigger injectors, too- would you need to equalize air flow between all cylinders?<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.shawnrocks.com/Animation1.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||JohnnyK||08-14-2001||02:01 AM||||Well.. You have the v6, so there are no throttle bodies.. (or carbs).. The best you could do is, well, six larger injectors..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||olympic||08-14-2001||03:58 AM|||| A friend of mine did this on a V8.  But instead of 8-1 barrel carbs, he used 4-2 barrel carbs.  He made his own intake out of sheet metal and steel pipe.  It looked awesome but tuning the 4 carbs to work together properly was a nightmare.||||reg||1
Z||000003||artherd||08-14-2001||06:14 AM||||"Individual Throttle butterflies per cylender" (or such)   Any ulitmate performance engine uses such a setup, and it's really really cool :)<P>IMHO, why bother with it for the 2.8 though, it's not exactly a stellar engine...<P>I would like to see a 'velocity stack' with individual butterflies for the Northstar motor though.  Perhaps I will have to make my own.<P>PS: Sync between all the butterflies is critical, and most have tiny 'cheater' equalization pipes that are effective only at idle to keep mixtures even at very small/no opening.<P>PS: there are several velocity stack manifolds for checy 350 V8s....<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000004||Slammed Fiero||08-14-2001||08:23 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by JohnnyK:<BR><B>Well.. You have the v6, so there are no throttle bodies.. (or carbs).. The best you could do is, well, six larger injectors..   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I could swear that little metal butterfly type unit on a V6 with "Holley" writen on it is a Throttle body.<P><BR>In anycase...<P>try TWM induction , they built the setup for our 911 (6 TB's) looks like Webers /Deloroto's ...ect. Increased upper end power (Read massive gains) I Had thought of doing this several times. Use the lower and middle manifold. Then off of the middle manifold adapt your TB's , there are lots of various kinds out there , it's just a matter of finding the right equation for power. Would be a really nice setup , I think you would lose low end power , but the upper end gains would be well worth it.  Would be nice to see a hole in the decklid with 2 Box filters and 6 stacks poking out...<P>Could always go cheaper route and do 3 2 Downdraft webers. Be prepared to tune it quite often.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>JM <P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Wannabe||08-14-2001||08:45 AM||||I spent days looking for an intake manifold that would allow mounting of three double or two triple Weber carbs but there appears to be nothing available for the V660. A racing buddy told me he had seen such a set up in action. With that kind of intake setup, you could go wild with the camshaft and conceivably get close to 300 hp. Race only mind, you I doubt it would be very streetable.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Kasdan||08-14-2001||09:20 AM||||Funny, i have that little unit with Holley written on it, i could have sworn that was my throddle body...maybe thats my a/c compressor?||||reg||1
Z||000007||rc5star||08-14-2001||10:26 AM||||Has anyone ever tried to design up a different middle and upper intake that would mount to a bored out throttle body? <P>My thoughts were if you: <BR>1. ported and polished your lower intake <BR>2. designed a middle and upper intake with larger ports that matched up to the lower intake and hooked into a bored out TB you would increase air flow.<P>May just be the crack pipe taking.....<p>[This message has been edited by rc5star (edited 08-14-2001).]||||reg||3
Z||000008||Slammed Fiero||08-14-2001||10:36 AM||||DOH!<P>Ryan Falconer had a setup for 60 degree  engines to run Webbers (SU's?) He ran them on Baja engines.<P>Now ...Get a hold of the manifold , and the rest is pretty easy. The mecahnical part doesn't scare me , the computer does.<P>Figure out using items like a HAL AF30 , APEXi Fuel computer and such your optimum air fuel ratio. Get a hold of TWM induction, and get a setup designed to flow that amount of air. Adjustable Fuel pressure regulator.<P>Need dyno time to get it working right. But that manifold is out there. I will be home tonight , I have a picture of it on a motor , it's whats called a swan neck setup , the TB's or carbs are not verticle , but on an angle... Very exotic looking<P>is Falconer Industries still around?? Anyone try Huffaker??<P>JM ||||reg||1
Z||000009||JohnnyK||08-14-2001||01:54 PM||||Alright.. Jesus.. I didn't think the v6 had a TBI...||||reg||1
Z||000010||Shaun41178||08-14-2001||05:15 PM||||On the cover of the Chevrolet Power manual I believe that is a 60 degree engine on it.  If it isn't then in the manual in the 60 degree section there is an intake manifold in there with 6 individual velocity stacks that are pretty much 6 individual TB's.  It was a complete intake manifolds setup.  So its out there but good luck finding it.<P>Johnny the V6 Fiero does not have TBI(Throttle Body Injection) but it does have a TB on it.  The 4 cyl has TBI however<P>I would try the companies that Slammed recommended or look in the Chevrolet book and see what the book says about who made that intake setup and then give them a call.<P>------------------<BR>Shaun 85 GT with nitrous<BR>0-60 in 5.6 seconds||||reg||1
Z||000011||85Josh||08-14-2001||07:37 PM||||Johnny, it dosen't, but all fuel injection systems have to meter the air somehow.<p>[This message has been edited by 85Josh (edited 08-14-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000012||theogre||08-14-2001||08:41 PM||||If it can be done with the type of EFI Fiero V6 uses, it won't be easy or cheap.<P>A big item is figuring out how to plumb the MAP sensor. MAP is used for fuel and timing calculations.<P>Doing it with carbs is not too fun either. Synchronizing carburators is a pain. Just ask motorcycle mechanics.... They have to do allot of this.||||reg||1
Z||000013||terryk||08-14-2001||09:55 PM||||Nah, it just takes 6 Uni-sync's and the patience of a kindergarden teacher.....||||reg||1
Z||000014||Cooter||08-14-2001||10:09 PM||||Did someone call a kindergarten teacher?||||reg||1
